From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:45:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 106/111] A view shows a document once, like Notepad++

Moving or dragging a clone into the view that already holds its twin
put two tabs of one document side by side in one tab bar. Now the moved
clone closes and its twin is shown. Clone to other view, when the other
view already holds a clone, shows that clone instead of opening another.
Only clones that mirror each other and hold the same text count; clones
whose restored drafts drifted apart are left as they are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

